# Vulnerabilities formally accepted for the Trivy gate (cd.yml). Each entry needs a reason and an expiry date.
# Security plan: docs/documentation-technique.md, sections 5.2 and 5.3 (decision SEC01).

# CVE-2026-47884 (CRITICAL), spring-webmvc 6.2.19: path limitation flaw in XsltView.
# - MicroCRM does not use XsltView (the API only serves JSON through Spring Data REST).
# - No free fix in Spring Framework 6.x: only 7.0.9+, i.e. Spring Boot 4 (planned major upgrade, section 8).
# - Accepted until the Spring Boot 4 upgrade, at the latest 2027-01-31; the gate blocks again after that date.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31

# CVE-2026-47890 (CRITICAL), spring-webmvc 6.2.19: Server-Sent Events stream corruption when rendering view fragments.
# - MicroCRM uses no Server-Sent Events and no view fragments (pure JSON through Spring Data REST; checked in back/src).
# - No free fix in Spring Framework 6.x: only 7.0.9+, i.e. Spring Boot 4 (planned major upgrade, section 8).
# - Accepted on the same terms as above, at the latest until 2027-01-31.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
